<title>USA: Nissan recalls 20,500 '95 Quest minivans.</title>
<headline>Nissan recalls 20,500 '95 Quest minivans.</headline>
<dateline>CARSON, Calif. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Copr U.S.A. said Wednesday it is recalling 20,500 1995 Quest minivans for possible problems with the rear lamp.</p>
<p>The vehicles were made between April 1995 and September 1995. Nissan, a unit of Nissan Motor Co Ltd, said the rear lamp may not illuminate because the metal connection in the socket moves or separates from the plastic housing.</p>
<p>The problem can result in the stop/tail combination lamp or turn signal lamp not functioning. The center high mounted stop lamp operation is not affected, said Nissan.</p>
</text>
